X-Harness-Test-Only: commit=8de23a18b9d4c74cc04abb8cca82fbcc106f0bf5 parent=2aa5e747fa35058bb27e7f632839ddc2073710f7 tree=d49aac556737f4aad937621269237cfc004ebcd7
Subject: [PATCH] test(cli): ACP sends no placeholder bearer and pins Bedrock
 IAM auth (red first)

Test-only commit for fork patch 0007. With CLINE_API_KEY set to a placeholder,
an ambient bogus AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK and role credentials in the default
chain:

- a Bedrock session opens without a Cline credential; the Cline provider still
  requires authentication;
- ACP does not forward CLINE_API_KEY to Bedrock and pins aws.authentication
  "iam" on top of the stored settings, unless providers.json explicitly chose
  api-key; the Cline provider still receives CLINE_API_KEY;
- wire test through ACP buildConfig, core createAgentModelFromConfig, the real
  Bedrock vendor and a stubbed fetch: Authorization is
  "AWS4-HMAC-SHA256 Credential=<role key>/<date>/us-west-2/bedrock/aws4_request"
  and no header carries the placeholder or the ambient bearer.

Rebased onto cli-v3.0.71 (test files taken from the rebased fork patch 0006, old number 0007).
